<article class="env-lemma" id="00H1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00H1">Lemma <span data-tag="00H1">10.37.14</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a normal ring. Then $R[x]$ is a normal ring. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\mathfrak q$ be a prime of $R[x]$. Set $\mathfrak p = R \cap \mathfrak q$. Then we see that $R_{\mathfrak p}[x]$ is a normal domain by Lemma <a href="/tag/030A" data-tag="030A">10.37.8</a>. Hence $(R[x])_{\mathfrak q}$ is a normal domain by Lemma <a href="/tag/00GY" data-tag="00GY">10.37.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>